  "cross_rung_agreement_is_an_internal_consistency_check": "the rungs are computed from the SAME nuclei and are NOT statistically independent, so their agreement cannot rule out an error common to the data. It tests only that the model's functional form holds across aggregation scales, since the algebra involves k explicitly. max_over_min_ratio <= 2 is the declared bound. Disagreement is informative; agreement is not replication.",
